\title{Separable polynomial}
\taxon{Definition}
\date{2023-10-01}
\author{JB00}
\import{macros}

\p{An irreducible polynomial #{f \in K[X]} is \em{separable} if it splits into distinct linear factors in a splitting field.}

\p{The convention in this course is that we use the same definition for any #{0 \neq f \in K[X]}.}

\p{Anything which is not separable is called \em{inseparable}.}
